<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27431" root="طيح" body-key="T">
    
      1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَاحَ</span></b> , aor. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَطِيحُ</span>, inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَيْحٌ</span>: see 1 in art.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طوح</span>. Sb says that this verb is [originally <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَوِحَ</span>,
aor. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَطْوِحُ</span>, i. e.,] of the measure <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَعِلَ</span>, aor. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَفْعِلُ</span>;
like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَلِىَ</span>, aor. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَلِى</span>; accord. to those who say
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَوَّحَهُ</span>, and not <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَيَّحَهُ</span>: but accord. to those who
say <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَيَّحَهُ</span>, it is [originally <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَيَحَ</span>, aor. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَطْيِحُ</span>, of
the measure <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَعَلَ</span>, aor. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَفْعِلُ</span>,] like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَاعَ</span>, aor. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَبِيعُ</span>.
(L, TA.)

